{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Let now a little water be taken.</b> Rashi explained that he did not wish to bring idolatry into his house. And this is far from reason — for because of fools who corrupted it, would he not bring any dust at all into his house? And why would he bring the light of the sun into his house, when there are many who worship the sun? Rather, it is not prohibited in any case — just as the earth of the world is not prohibited. And it is more plausible to hear that he did not wish to give of his bread to those who are unfit, for perhaps they are Arabs; therefore he wished to bring them back in repentance through their removing the foreign god from within them, for idolatry is satisfied with nullification of any sort. Therefore it says ״מְעַט מַיִם,״ and it says ״יֻקַּח״ — in the passive, meaning through another, for even if they remove the dust, what of it, if one faith is negated — will another remain fixed in their hearts? And purity of the heart is a matter not in the hand of Abraham; therefore ״יֻקַּח מְעַט מַיִם״ — pure waters, to purify the hearts, for this matter is given over to them and not to him." "And by way of allusion it appears to say: concerning this he said ״וְהִשָּׁעֲנוּ תַּחַת הָעֵץ,״ for he should have said ״וְהִשָּׁעֲנוּ בָּעֵץ״; rather, he wanted to say: 'Come, take shelter in the shadow of Shaddai,' as Rashi explained on the verse ״סָר צִלָּם״ (Numbers 14:9) — that is, the shadow of the Holy One, blessed be He. And so there are some who explain along the path of Kabbalah that the statement ״הֲיֵשׁ בָּהּ עֵץ אִם אַיִן״ (Numbers 13:20) resembles what is said (Exodus 17:7) ״הֲיֵשׁ ה׳ בְּקִרְבֵּנוּ אִם אָיִן.״ Thus he said to them: lean for yourselves under the tree that makes shade, alluding to the true shadow in whose shadow all existing beings live — וְהַמַּשְׂכִּיל יָבִין. And some say: because the earth brings everything into existence, for everything comes from the dust and thither everything returns, therefore they erred to say that there is in it an aspect of divinity."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:28:42.059894703Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}